 "/results/2194"} "Nordic combined"] " and cross-country skiing. They were not unique from this event, as the Pole " [:a {:href "/athletes/84958"} "Bronisław Czech"] " is the only known Olympian to have competed in five different sports (or disciplines), competing in " [:a {:href "/results/1166"} "Alpine skiing"] ", cross-country skiing, Nordic combined, ski jumping, and the military ski patrol. He would become a resistance fighter during World War II, and sadly died from typhus while held at the Auschwitz-Birkenau concentration camp."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Norway"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "3-50:47.0"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "9"} [:a {:href "/athletes/74214"} "Ole Reistad"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900554"} "Leif Skagnæs"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/97822"} "Ole Stenen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/99302"} "Reidar Ødegård"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Finland"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "3-54:37.0"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "9"} [:a {:href "/athletes/900194"} "Eino Kuvaja"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900209"} "Kalle Tuppurainen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/87700"} "Esko Järvinen"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/900204"} "Veikko Ruotsalainen"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "Switzerland"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://oly